USOS 3.1.2-usos10 patch 11/11 (2026-10-15): read-only KeTickCount watcher on the BIOS helper core (diagnostic, Windows 2000 ACPI flow only)

Windows 2000 SP4 with the ACPI HAL on the ASRock X470 (no CSM) reaches
kernel phase 1 (usosvid row 11) and then stalls; usosvid's heartbeat never
draws. Step A (patch 0007) ruled out an SMI rewriting RTC A/B. This patch
answers the next question independently of Windows DPCs: does KeTickCount
(the clock interrupt) still advance?

Only with csmwrap.ini acpi_legacy_fadt = true (written only for the
Windows 2000 ACPI flow, tools/xp_csmwrap_esp.sh); otherwise the trampoline
argument is 0 and the helper keeps the old MWAIT/PAUSE loop.

- EFI (src/usos_watcher_efi.c): validated FADT (the RSDT copy found as in
  patch 0007) -> PM1a_EVT/PM1a_CNT/PM_TMR/GPE0 ports (legacy fields, GAS
  System I/O fallback); TSC calibrated against the PM timer (~100 ms,
  bounded); one 4 KiB EfiReservedMemoryType page below 4 GiB; after
  build_e820_map the page must be wholly covered by E820 type 2 entries
  (usw_e820_reserved) or the watcher stays off; its PA goes to the helper
  through a private trampoline dword (EDX), not through CSMPPrxy, and to BDA
  0x4FC-0x4FF right before Legacy16Boot (0x4F4-0x4FB = step A untouched).
- Helper (seabios/src/romlayout.S, usos_watch.c): PAUSE + RDTSC deadline
  instead of MWAIT; request_pending is checked on every iteration and served
  before the next sample (CSMPPrxy ABI unchanged). About once a second: Tick
  low and KUSER_SHARED_DATA InterruptTime low (physical addresses published
  by usosvid 1.3), PM1_STS/PM1_EN/PM1_CNT, GPE0 STS/EN (bytewise), PIC IMRs
  (data ports), written to the page (helper range 0x100-0x1FF) and as one
  80-column line on VGA text row 24.
- Reads only: no OUT/W1C, no SMI_CMD, no EOI/OCW, no IOREGSEL/IOWIN, no CMOS,
  no LAPIC/IPI. Writes: the reserved page and VGA row 24.
- If a proxied BIOS function never returns, the watcher stops with it.

Design, code and QEMU q35 runs by Codex (2026-10-15, as its patch 0008 on
usos6); applied unchanged on top of usos9 patches 0001-0010 for usos10.
Own code: shared/EFI parts LGPL-2.1-or-later, SeaBIOS part LGPL-3.0-or-later.
No Microsoft code in the patch. KeTickCount/KUSER_SHARED_DATA offsets come
from the DDK headers and the SP4 binaries; the earlier diagnosis rounds also
used the user-supplied NT5 source material as a map of HAL/kernel behaviour,
so this is not a clean-room claim (docs/windows-2000-acpi-x470-2026-10-12.md).

